#: INTRO.md:11
msgid "Scientific context"
msgstr "科学的背景"

#: INTRO.md:13
msgid ""
"Magnesium(II) ions are abundant in living cells and they interact with RNA "
"molecules, modulating their folding, catalytic properties and structural "
"dynamics. Mg<sup>2+</sup> are found to coordinate in the inner sphere of "
"several RNA moieties, non-bridging phosphate oxygen atoms (OP1, OP2) being "
"by and large the most frequent in PDB structures and having the strongest "
"binding affinity [[1, 2]](#references)."
msgstr ""
"Magnesium(II) Ion は生細胞に豊富に存在し、RNA と相互作用して Folding、触媒特性、構造 Dynamics "
"を調節します。Mg<sup>2+</sup> は RNA のさまざまな部位に Inner Sphere で配位します。PDB 構造では Non-"
"bridging Phosphate Oxygen (OP1, OP2) が圧倒的に多く、最も強い結合親和性を持ちます [[1, "
"2]](#references)。"

#: INTRO.md:15
msgid ""
"Due to its high charge density, Mg<sup>2+</sup> strongly interacts with "
"innersphere ligands, resulting in slow (sub-microsecond) water-exchange "
"kinetics compared to other biologically abundant cations, and even slower "
"binding to phosphate groups [[3]](#references). This feature is amplified in"
" most Molecular Dynamics force fields, which hinders satisfactiory sampling "
"of the equilibrium properties of Mg-RNA interactions."
msgstr ""
"Mg<sup>2+</sup> は電荷密度が高いため Inner-sphere Ligand と強く相互作用し、生体内に豊富なほかの Cation "
"と比べて Water Exchange の Kinetics が遅く（Sub-microsecond）、Phosphate "
"基への結合はさらに遅くなります [[3]](#references)。多くの Molecular Dynamics Force Field "
"ではこの特徴が増幅され、Mg-RNA 相互作用の平衡特性を十分に Sampling することが難しくなります。"

#: INTRO.md:17
msgid ""
"While force-field parameters can be designed in order to accelerate the slow"
" dynamics of magnesium, it is unclear whether the limited flexibility of "
"classical MD potentials allow for selective tuning of the kinetics without "
"compromising other quantities of interest, such as thermodynamics and "
"geometric properties. In this tutorial we will explore another approach, "
"where we selectively bias the MD simulation to accelerate the process of "
"interest, and that can be adapted in principle to any force field."
msgstr ""
"Magnesium の遅い Dynamics を加速する Force Field パラメータも設計できますが、古典 MD Potential "
"の限られた柔軟性で、Thermodynamics や幾何学的特性を損なわず Kinetics だけを調整できるかは不明です。この Tutorial "
"では別の方法として、MD に選択的に Bias を加えて目的の過程を加速します。原理的には任意の Force Field に適用できます。"

#: INTRO.md:19
msgid "Outline"
msgstr "構成"

#: INTRO.md:21
msgid ""
"In [Part 1](PART1.md) we will set up a model dinucleotide and use well-"
"tempered metadynamics to characterize the binding free-energy landscape of "
"Mg<sup>2+</sup> to non-bridging phosphate oxygens of the RNA backbone."
msgstr ""
"[Part 1](PART1.md) ではモデル Dinucleotide を準備し、Well-tempered Metadynamics で "
"Mg<sup>2+</sup> と RNA Backbone の Non-bridging Phosphate Oxygen "
"の結合自由エネルギー地形を調べます。"

#: INTRO.md:23
msgid ""
"In [Part 2](PART2.md) we will use the previous simulation to design a "
"biasing potential that selectively accelerates the binding kinetics."
msgstr ""
"[Part 2](PART2.md) では前のシミュレーションを使い、結合 Kinetics を選択的に加速する BiasPotential "
"を設計します。"

#: INTRO.md:25
msgid ""
"In Part 3 we will see how to apply the method to a larger system using "
"Hamiltonian replica exchange."
msgstr "Part 3 では、Hamiltonian Replica Exchange を使って、より大きな系に適用する方法を見ます。"

